ion of Section 3 exhibits a tiling that uses exactly $2n-2$ tiles.  Therefore the minimum possible number of tiles is\\n\\\\[\\nf(n)=2n-2.\\n\\\\]\\nFor $n=2025$ we obtain\\n\\\\[\\nf(2025)=2\\\\cdot2025-2=4048.\\n\\\\]\\nThus Matilda can achieve the required condition with $4048$ tiles, and it is impossible to do so with fewer.\\n\\n---\\n**Answer:** $\\\\boxed{4048}$\\n\",\n  \"final_answer\": \"4048\"\n}"
